       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is 5 times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg/day. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I know of no indication that supports it. Doses that high carry a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and confirming the number doesn't change that risk.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Dose was a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Dose is deliberate:** Please discuss it with your attending and pharmacy. If they approve, send me the rationale and who approved it. I can then enter the order with that documented in the note, though I'd still want to understand the indication first.\n- **Dose above 200 mg is needed:** I can enter the maximum of 200 mg once daily, and you can titrate from there."
      }
     ],
